{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/702159-an-average-session-at-court","id":702159,"title":"An average session at Court","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-15T08:41:01-07:00","id":702159,"title":"An average session at Court","content":"Good morning folks. Could some one help me outline a typical generic session of Court? I know major players are expected to be there (prince, seneschal, etc/ etc.) but who else is expected to be there? Is there an organized flow chart of subjects that bust be gone over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8545-horatio80","name":"Horatio80","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T08:57:58-07:00","id":702215,"title":"","content":"How court is held is a great opportunity to showcase the thematic differences between the Covenants.<br /> <br /> Me personal 'generic' court would probably be in the 1E Invictus style, and be something like:<ul><li>Minions / Ghouls and Retainers set up the chosen Elysium or Court Location during the day.</li> <li>Doors open an hour after dark.</li> <li>Low-Status Kindred filter in first.</li> <li>Higher Status Kindred and Officers filter in later - possible with an official presentation by a minion or neonate, &quot;Presenting the Alder Sebastian Maddox of the First Esate,&quot; &quot;Presenting the Prince's Harpy, Madame Renata Martell of the Order of Dracula.&quot;</li> <li>The Prince or Praxis Holder(s) come in last.</li> <li>Break for a presentation, performance, entertainment or other &quot;fun&quot; scene.</li> <li>Official business begins in reverse order - The Prince makes their own proclamations, law announcements, land grants, etc. Then, the next most important officer does the same, and so on.</li> <li>Depending on the status/demeanor of the Prince, they might walk out at some point and allow their Seneschal or Primogen/Prisci Councils to continue further (non-important) business.</li> <li>General mingling, deal making and politics after official business is concluded.</li> <li>Some sort of formal 'ending announcement' at the end of the night.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:10:36-07:00","id":702228,"title":"","content":"As far as general subjects touched upon in business, below might be common things:<ul><li>Prince:<ul><li>Proclaiming New Laws or Traditions</li> <li>Issuing Punishments</li> <li>Issuing Rewards<ul><li>Appointing / Removing Officers</li> <li>Granting / Removing Domains</li> <li>Granting / Removing Feeding Rights</li> <li>Granting / Removing Status</li> <li>Granting Rights of Progeny</li> <li>Blood Hunts</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Sheriff<ul><li>Warnings of New Danger or Crimes</li> <li>Trials of Accused Lawbreakers (Judicial or -by-Combat)</li> <li>Appointing / Removing Deputies</li> </ul></li> <li>Keeper / Master of Elysium<ul><li>Declaring / Revoking official Elysia</li> <li>Stripping Status from Elysium violators</li> </ul></li> <li>Harpies<ul><li>Granting / Removing Status</li> <li>Adjudicating Boons / Prestation</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> And of course, any interesting political pressures or concerns the Primogen or Prisci Councils might want to levy on the Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T12:24:48-07:00","id":702434,"title":"","content":"As Holy notes, it depends very much on the individual Prince or equivalent and other title-holders, if any.<br /> <br /> A regular meeting in Elysium will typically include time for proclamations, and for vampires to approach their leaders with other business, but anything else will vary.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/82661/Invite-Only\" target=\"_blank\">Invite Only</a> covers court and other Kindred social gatherings, with suggestions and ready-to-use examples of Elysium locations and events.<br /> <br /> Holy's example would work well for a strictly formalised court in a large city. For more examples, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28796/Damnation-City\" target=\"_blank\">Damnation City</a> has a section on ten very different Princes, whose courts would be equally different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T12:28:17-07:00","id":702439,"title":"","content":"I think Holy covered the standard skeleton pretty comprehensively. I'd guess in many courts there might be an opportunity to air grievances, and that could either be exceedingly formal (Covenant or Clan members confer with their Primogen who then brings to the court the issues he sees fit) or more of a town hall free-for-all, depending on the Covenant and Prince in power.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I'd just use the basic court as an outline. Every city is different, and every Prince rules differently. Damnation City shows some good case examples of how different Princes might assert their authority. I'd look at who your Prince is, how they operate, and what kind of meetings that would lead to. I think with a lot of Princes, most of the actual decision making is done behind closed doors, and the formality of the actual court is just pomp and circumstance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T16:22:14-07:00","id":702597,"title":"","content":"I think Holy pretty much nails it. Some details of the court might work differently, if the prince is not Invictus. But the outline is a very good basis.<br /> <br /> Just one minor nitpick: since VtR2 divests Status completely from Title in the Kindred community, I think the harpies (and maybe the keeper) are sole purveyors of Status. In the end, even a Prince could have Status 1 or 2, if the harpies aren't particularly impressed by him. So, I don't think s/he has any business granting or removing Status. Rather Status is gained or lost as consequence of his rewards or punishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T17:28:00-07:00","id":704052,"title":"","content":"<br /> I would call Holy's post an official court. I also like holding gatherings that less formal, Usually analogous to a mortal function, Art shows, debates or salons, evenings at museums and aquariums, events clubs or concert. If I feel really mean the event is front of mortals with the understanding the masquerade WILL be maintained!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}